# Rhett's PC Tweaks & Optimization

A colorful, keyboard-driven menu for tuning Windows. Pick a category, pick a tweak, press **Y** to apply it, **U** to undo it, or **N** to cancel. It is a single `.bat` file, so there is nothing to install.

> **Use at your own risk.** These tweaks change Windows settings. Create a restore point first (option **R** on the main menu). Every tweak can be previewed before you confirm it, and almost all of them can be undone from the same menu.

---

## Download

**Recommended:** go to the [**Releases page**](../../releases/latest) and download `Rhetts-PC-Tweaks.bat`.

**Or:** click the green **Code** button at the top of this page, choose **Download ZIP**, then extract it.

---

## Install and run (step by step)

No installer is needed. You just download the file and run it.

1. **Download** `Rhetts-PC-Tweaks.bat` using one of the options above.
2. **Extract it** if you downloaded the ZIP: right-click the ZIP, choose **Extract All**, then open the folder.
3. **Double-click** `Rhetts-PC-Tweaks.bat`.
4. **If Windows shows a blue "Windows protected your PC" screen:** click **More info**, then **Run anyway**. This appears for any unsigned script you download. You can read the whole file in Notepad first (right-click, **Edit**) if you want to see exactly what it does.
5. **Click Yes** on the "Do you want to allow this app to make changes" prompt. The tweaks need administrator rights.
6. **Press R** to create a System Restore Point before changing anything.
7. **Press a number key** (1 to 8) to open a category, then **press a letter key** to choose a tweak.
8. **Press Y** to apply it, **U** to undo it, or **N** to cancel.
9. **Restart your PC** after you are done. Some tweaks only take effect after a reboot.

### If the file will not run

- Right-click the `.bat` file, choose **Properties**, tick **Unblock** at the bottom, click **OK**, then try again.
- Right-click the file and choose **Run as administrator**.
- If your antivirus blocks it, the file is a plain-text script that edits registry values and Windows settings, which some security tools flag by default. Read the file yourself and allow it only if you are comfortable.

---

## What is inside

| Key | Category | What it does |
|-----|----------|--------------|
| 1 | **Network** | Flush DNS, renew IP, reset Winsock and TCP/IP, Cloudflare or Google DNS, TCP tuning, remove throttling, disable Nagle, adapter power saving, QoS, Delivery Optimization |
| 2 | **CPU** | Foreground priority boost, core parking off, minimum processor state, power throttling off, system responsiveness, CPU info |
| 3 | **GPU** | GPU scheduling (HAGS), Multiplane Overlay, fullscreen optimizations, windowed-game and VRR settings, driver timeout, shader cache clear |
| 4 | **Memory** | SysMain, keep kernel in RAM, memory compression, page combining, NTFS memory usage, RAM info |
| 5 | **Performance** | Ultimate Performance plan, **Rhett's Performance** (all-in-one), High Performance plan, visuals, startup and shutdown speed, TRIM |
| 6 | **Gaming** | Game Mode, Game DVR, mouse acceleration, game task priority |
| 7 | **Privacy** | Advertising ID, telemetry, DiagTrack, activity history, Start suggestions, web search |
| 8 | **Cleanup** | Temp files, Recycle Bin, update cache, thumbnails, SFC, DISM |
| R | **Restore point** | Creates a System Restore Point |

### Rhett's Performance

Found under **5 Performance**, option **B**. It builds a custom power plan called **Rhett's Performance** and applies a bundle of safe CPU, GPU, network, gaming and system tweaks in one go.

- Keeps all CPU cores awake and the CPU at full speed, and turns off disk, USB and PCIe power saving.
- Applies the CPU, GPU, network, gaming, startup, shutdown and disk tweaks listed above.
- Applies the RAM tweaks only if you have about 16 GB of RAM or more.
- Only disables SysMain if no hard drive is detected.
- Leaves hibernation and mouse acceleration alone.
- Press **U** on it to revert everything it changed and delete the custom plan.

The power plan settings apply when plugged in. A laptop on battery keeps its normal limits.

---

## Requirements

- Windows 10 or Windows 11
- Administrator rights
- Nothing else. PowerShell, which ships with Windows, is used for a few of the tweaks.

## Undoing changes

- Run the script, open the same tweak, and press **U**.
- Or use **System Restore** from the Start menu and pick the restore point you created with **R**.

## Troubleshooting

| Problem | Fix |
|---------|-----|
| Strange characters like `[96m` on screen | Your console does not support colors. Use Windows Terminal or update Windows 10 to a recent version. |
| Window opens and closes right away | Right-click the file and choose **Run as administrator**. |
| A tweak says it needs a reboot | Restart Windows. |
| Something feels off after a tweak | Open the tweak again and press **U**, or use your restore point. |

